-09-24T06:13:03.059Z","text":"Artwork like a hut would be good","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-24T06:13:03.059Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T21:08:48.174Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-24.1","cardId":"ODY-073","number":73,"name":"Olive-Oil Lamp","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-24T06:16:58.958Z","text":"Artwork not working","context":""},{"at":"2026-09-24T06:17:20.649Z","text":"Sorry, artwork too small","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-24T06:16:58.958Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T21:08:48.227Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-24.1","cardId":"ODY-074","number":74,"name":"Set Bread Before the Guest","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-24T06:17:50.431Z","text":"Artwork sounds perfect","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-24T06:17:50.431Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T21:08:48.289Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.14","cardId":"ODY-074","number":74,"name":"Duel of Hector and Ajax","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-27T11:12:19.697Z","text":"Weird design, don't see the use case","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-27T11:12:19.697Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-27T11:49:56.240Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-074","number":74,"name":"Duel of Hector and Ajax","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T09:49:22.123Z","text":"A fight that rewards both creature surviving, that would mean the card failed as a removal so I expect this to be pretty bad.","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T09:49:22.123Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T09:49:22.123Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-24.1","cardId":"ODY-077","number":77,"name":"Phaeacian Oarsman","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-24T06:19:29.266Z","text":"Need better art","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-24T06:19:29.266Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T21:08:48.340Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-24.1","cardId":"ODY-078","number":78,"name":"Odysseus's Cloak and Brooch","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-24T06:20:26.915Z","text":"Potentially could use better artwork","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-24T06:20:26.915Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T21:08:48.391Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-24.1","cardId":"ODY-079","number":79,"name":"Demodocus, Blind Singer","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-24T06:22:24.395Z","text":"Better artwork","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-24T06:22:24.395Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T21:08:48.466Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-24.1","cardId":"ODY-084","number":84,"name":"Hearthfire Cook","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-24T06:28:21.016Z","text":"Artwork sounds perfect, doesn't resolve","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-24T06:28:21.016Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T21:08:48.539Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-24.1","cardId":"ODY-085","number":85,"name":"Beach-Drawn Longship","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-24T06:28:49.744Z","text":"Needs better artwork","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-24T06:28:49.744Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T21:08:48.595Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-24.1","cardId":"ODY-087","number":87,"name":"Seabird Lookout","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-24T06:29:58.572Z","text":"Needs to be an ancient sailor looking out","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-24T06:29:58.572Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T21:08:48.650Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-24.1","cardId":"ODY-092","number":92,"name":"Vengeance in the Great Hall","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-24T10:36:57.989Z","text":"This scene doesn't really feel red white to me, nor are the modes interesting","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-24T10:36:57.989Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T21:08:48.727Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-24.1","cardId":"ODY-093","number":93,"name":"Ordeal of the Bow","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-24T10:38:46.532Z","text":"Needs an artwork related to the bow contest","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-24T10:38:46.532Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T21:08:48.798Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.14","cardId":"ODY-093","number":93,"name":"Ordeal of the Suitors","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-27T03:50:42.938Z","text":"For are survival, have we decided this wording works, or do we need to give the creature survival?","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-27T03:50:42.938Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-27T04:46:17.579Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-24.1","cardId":"ODY-094","number":94,"name":"Laertes' Final Spear","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-24T10:39:37.826Z","text":"Need a relevant unique artwork","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-24T10:39:37.826Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-24T21:08:48.857Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.14","cardId":"ODY-094","number":94,"name":"Laertes' Final Spear","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-27T04:12:17.802Z","text":"Adapt this reprint for Odyssey, new card","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-27T04:12:17.802Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-27T04:46:17.630Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-094","number":94,"name":"Laertes' Final Spear","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T05:48:56.434Z","text":"adapt to original","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T05:48:56.434Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T09:41:32.346Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.14","cardId":"ODY-098","number":98,"name":"Boar Hunt on Parnassus","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-27T04:14:50.178Z","text":"Need to work on wording, could be an aura","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-27T04:14:50.178Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:01:14.821Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-104","number":104,"name":"Hide the Weapons","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T05:48:12.904Z","text":"Can use stun counters here, need to watch out for how many times we tap to creatures as an effect, seems we're using that a lot","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T05:48:12.904Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T05:48:12.904Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.14","cardId":"ODY-107","number":107,"name":"The Walls of Troy","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-27T04:16:54.075Z","text":"How big does this wall need to be to be worth 5?","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-27T04:16:54.075Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:01:19.896Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-110","number":110,"name":"Andromache's Farewell","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T10:05:51.231Z","text":"+2/+2 would have more utility towards dying / trading","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T10:05:51.231Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T10:05:51.231Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-111","number":111,"name":"Faithful Old Hound","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T10:06:32.883Z","text":"This is a duplicate of Argos, can be removed, but lets use this artwork for Argos","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T10:06:32.883Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T10:06:32.883Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.14","cardId":"ODY-113","number":113,"name":"Grip of Charybdis","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-27T04:21:25.677Z","text":"Adapt this for Odyssey, consider rate improvement precedent in the mean time, and or a an additional little effect","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-27T04:21:25.677Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:01:24.984Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-113","number":113,"name":"Grip of Charybdis","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T10:07:09.432Z","text":"Redesign for Odyssey","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T10:07:09.432Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T10:07:09.432Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-114","number":114,"name":"Holy Moly","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T10:08:00.813Z","text":"This is no longer a reprint of Annul, so doesn't need to reference the card","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T10:08:00.813Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T10:08:00.813Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.14","cardId":"ODY-122","number":122,"name":"Hector Falls","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-27T04:25:05.423Z","text":"Hero's Fall or something like that could be better,\nI mean, I know it's standard that we have a big fat black removal, I guess that's okay if this is it\nAlso good if we tweak it for Odysse and call it our own","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-27T04:25:05.423Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:01:30.064Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-122","number":122,"name":"Hector Falls","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T10:08:50.891Z","text":"I think this is no longer sip of hemlock","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T10:08:50.891Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T10:08:50.891Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-128","number":128,"name":"Laocoön's Serpents","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T10:10:11.839Z","text":"I think this needs to be in-timeline for Odyssey","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T10:10:11.839Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T10:10:11.839Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-135","number":135,"name":"Omen of the Bellowing Meat","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T10:11:08.441Z","text":"Needs to somehow feel like the meat of slaughtered sacred cows that has come alive and is bellowing and portends of bad things to come.","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T10:11:08.441Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T10:11:08.441Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-137","number":137,"name":"Limestone Goat","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T10:11:53.201Z","text":"Lets make this a pig","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T10:11:53.201Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T10:11:53.201Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.9","cardId":"ODY-144","number":144,"name":"Obol for the Dead","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-26T23:18:09.594Z","text":"Would it be better to redesign this in the same vein?","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-26T23:18:09.594Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:01:35.183Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-144","number":144,"name":"Obol for the Dead","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T05:48:43.303Z","text":"This is correctly trinket-sized, but we need to adapt the card for our set as an original","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T05:48:43.303Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T05:48:43.303Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.14","cardId":"ODY-149","number":149,"name":"Athena-Favored Night Raider","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-27T04:32:04.583Z","text":"Twist on favoured hoplite here","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-27T04:32:04.583Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:01:40.233Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-170","number":170,"name":"Seals on the Sunlit Rocks","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T10:15:28.834Z","text":"That's a fairly weak ability, not very flavourful","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T10:15:28.834Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T10:15:28.834Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-172","number":172,"name":"Hound's Protective Fury","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T10:15:56.851Z","text":"Flavour doesn't mean anything to me","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T10:15:56.851Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T10:15:56.851Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-183","number":183,"name":"Athena's Golden Lamp","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T02:20:36.400Z","text":"Need a trinket in this vein, but should arise from a very solid artwork source that renders an icon everyday object of the age","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T02:20:36.400Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T02:20:36.400Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-187","number":187,"name":"Scheria, Harbor of Strangers","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T10:16:57.763Z","text":"Needs to be it's own card in this register","context":""},{"at":"2026-09-30T10:17:32.584Z","text":"This is a duplicate","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T10:16:57.763Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T10:17:32.584Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-196","number":196,"name":"Palace of Circe","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T05:47:06.414Z","text":"Need to find something other than boar here","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T05:47:06.414Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T05:47:06.414Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-199","number":199,"name":"Penelope, Weaver of Fate","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T05:11:37.668Z","text":"Don't invent new counter, consider non counter approach, guess time could be flavourful","context":""},{"at":"2026-09-29T05:13:09.449Z","text":"What if she is like an ozolith for lore counters on sagas, survival triggers at the end of the turn, can move all counters on to or off of herself and a saga","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T05:11:37.668Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:01:45.309Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-201","number":201,"name":"Arms of Achilles","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T05:07:45.636Z","text":"Go back to shield of achilles, because the art is so perfect","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T05:07:45.636Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:02:27.040Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-204","number":204,"name":"Patroclus, Beloved Companion","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T05:04:29.296Z","text":"Artwork is Patraclus being tended by Achilles, like dead on, so the feeling of healing and your companion getting hurt should come through, could be an enrage ability or Survivor","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T05:04:29.296Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:02:29.084Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-210","number":210,"name":"Helios, All-Seeing Sun","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T04:54:45.968Z","text":"I think in general, this should be a sacrifice punisher, not trying to capture the whole episode again in a card","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T04:54:45.968Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:02:31.144Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-211","number":211,"name":"Hermes, Guide of Wanderers","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T04:53:23.319Z","text":"Flying, in general, we need to get flying in whereever it can go as there are not a lot of flavour opportunities","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T04:53:23.319Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:02:33.168Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-213","number":213,"name":"Olive-Wood Bed of Ithaca","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T04:51:27.342Z","text":"This should be like an artifact land enchantment, if the land it's on goes, then it's gone as well, otherwise it's very protected and provides a powerful defensive benefit","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T04:51:27.342Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:02:35.190Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-215","number":215,"name":"The Judgment of Paris","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T04:41:53.236Z","text":"I think this is not an episode that plays out over multiple beats and so should be treated as a single instance in which we are given the chance to choose one of the goddesses, the actually chosen goddess should be the most syngerstic and desirable in the context of the set","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T04:41:53.236Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:02:37.247Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-217","number":217,"name":"Metis, Cunning Counsel","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T04:38:55.164Z","text":"Whenever a permanent you control enters from exile,","context":""},{"at":"2026-09-29T04:39:56.784Z","text":"the first ability should work with Manifest Fate, also\nthe activated ability should trigger the triggered ability","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T04:38:55.164Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:02:39.287Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-218","number":218,"name":"Moira, Allotted Fate","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T04:37:51.544Z","text":"The virtues should all be 2 mana and set up a style of gameplay or build around","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T04:37:51.544Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:02:41.262Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-219","number":219,"name":"Eurymachus, Palacial Bully","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T04:36:05.736Z","text":"In the art, he is trowing a stool, somehow the name should indicate bully","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T04:36:05.736Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:03:00.202Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-222","number":222,"name":"Lotus-Eaters, Honeyed Hosts","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T04:23:14.987Z","text":"We have to capture this idea in a much more concise way, saga creatures have very limited text","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T04:23:14.987Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:03:02.247Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-232","number":232,"name":"Blood-Trench Lament","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T03:59:57.090Z","text":"This should feel like a ritual, sacrifice, gain, prophecy, blood, return","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T03:59:57.090Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:03:04.274Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.9","cardId":"ODY-233","number":233,"name":"Tityus, Ever-Tormented","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-27T00:00:39.521Z","text":"I'd like to redesign this into black to enchant an island and impersonate the bat from the second ixalan set, flipping the original","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-27T00:00:39.521Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:03:06.271Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-233","number":233,"name":"Ever-Tormented","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T02:02:25.024Z","text":"How would the name here be a reference to \"Chained to the Rocks\"?","context":""},{"at":"2026-09-30T05:53:56.822Z","text":"Need the flavourful rename here to make it look like it's continuing the cycle, good if it's homeric","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T02:02:25.024Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T05:53:56.822Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-237","number":237,"name":"Kleos, Deathless Renown","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T03:50:58.514Z","text":"The virture cycle needs to find ways of distingushing itself","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T03:50:58.514Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:03:08.371Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-238","number":238,"name":"Leucothea's Immortal Veil","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T03:43:52.829Z","text":"This art can be some sort of ancient veil artifact from related or any culture","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T03:43:52.829Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:03:11.319Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-239","number":239,"name":"Laertes's Orchard","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T03:50:01.979Z","text":"Unncessary unique counter type, I'm feeling like we have a number of enchantments that are actually lands, they could be enchantment lands","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T03:50:01.979Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:03:13.423Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-240","number":240,"name":"Circe, Self-Made Witch","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T03:48:27.120Z","text":"In general, we should prefer not to invent a new kind of counter for every time we want to achieve an effect like this, we need to use the available machinery to evoke the feeling we're after","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T03:48:27.120Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:03:15.468Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-240","number":240,"name":"Circe, Self-Made Witch","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T04:58:03.997Z","text":"This should be our Madeilline Miller Circe, she doesn't do pig stuff, she does something else related to her arc in the novel.","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T04:58:03.997Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T04:58:03.997Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-242","number":242,"name":"The House of Odysseus","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T03:45:24.357Z","text":"Potentially this is a land?","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T03:45:24.357Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:03:37.222Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-243","number":243,"name":"Bag of Winds","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T02:40:16.020Z","text":"It needs to feel a bit more volatile, like it's kind of beyond your control if the fail condition occurs, not something you knowingly build up to","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T02:40:16.020Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:03:39.283Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-245","number":245,"name":"Song of the Faithful Queen","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T02:37:13.580Z","text":"This flavour needs to more directly correspond to an actual work or purported song, it's too duplicative as is, could also be the imagined song of a relevant gods tale, or of a tale being told by the people of the world, but not of something that happens in main story","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T02:37:13.580Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:03:41.278Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-29.1","cardId":"ODY-245","number":245,"name":"Demodocus's Song of Ares and Aphrodite","status":"OPEN","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-30T02:23:48.202Z","text":"The hybrid saga cycle should be classic tales of Greek Gods","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-30T02:23:48.202Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-30T02:23:48.202Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-246","number":246,"name":"Helios's Vengeance","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T02:35:24.165Z","text":"Sacrifice doesn't make sense necessarily in this context, but you could try to make it make sense, I see the flavour advantage","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T02:35:24.165Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:03:43.295Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-247","number":247,"name":"Ogygia, Island Beyond Time","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T02:32:51.258Z","text":"Too complicated","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T02:32:51.258Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:03:45.391Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-249","number":249,"name":"The Long Way Home","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T02:29:54.986Z","text":"Could we invent a saga that has the potential for non-linear resolution while still not just be a RG machine - i.e. it feels meaningful, some amount of choice is involved, there is no choice to go directly to the end though, all of the cards complexity budget can be spen on this","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T02:29:54.986Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:03:47.382Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-269","number":269,"name":"Penelope's Upper Chamber","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T02:33:25.725Z","text":"Flavour redesign","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T02:33:25.725Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:03:49.402Z"},{"datasetVersion":"2026-09-26.35","cardId":"ODY-279","number":279,"name":"Communal Mixing Bowl","status":"RESOLVED","entries":[{"at":"2026-09-29T02:21:01.767Z","text":"This could be a food clue","context":""}],"createdAt":"2026-09-29T02:21:01.767Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-29T13:03:51.435Z"}]}